00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:14.370
What exactly is Cyber crime?

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:18.439
Nicole: Well, cyber crime which can
also be known as computer crime, is

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:23.060
the use of a computer or other digital
device and the internet to commit

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:27.079
illegal acts that may affect private
individuals, businesses, organisations

00:00:28.179 --> 00:00:32.150
and governments and can threaten
the overall security of the world.

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:35.699
Abraham: The use of new technologies
and the internet has given criminals

00:00:35.739 --> 00:00:39.519
a new tool for committing crime
which can subsequently take place

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:41.300
'virtually' anywhere in the world.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:45.879
Cyber crime is increasing all the
time and is becoming more complex

00:00:45.929 --> 00:00:50.090
affecting essential services,
companies and individuals whilst

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:52.159
also threatening national security.

00:00:53.209 --> 00:00:56.580
Nicole: Trying to cope with the
effects of cyber crime costs the

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:58.449
UK billions of pounds each year.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:03.670
The nature of cyber crime is that it's not
limited to a specific location and cyber

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:07.899
criminals can be based and commit their
crimes anywhere, making it difficult for

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:10.349
the police and security services to trace.

00:01:10.789 --> 00:01:14.110
However, cyber criminals do often
leave clues to their identity

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:18.530
and location and can be traced
by skilled cyber crime trackers.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:23.050
Abraham: The same skills used by the
cyber criminals can also be used by the

00:01:23.050 --> 00:01:25.460
police and security services to find them.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:30.329
Additionally, even if the criminal is
traced, if they are located in a different

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:34.640
part of the world, geopolitical issues
can mean it’s impossible or not worth

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:36.290
the effort to bring them to justice.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:40.820
It’s for these reasons there’s been a
huge increase of cyber crime, because

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:44.309
for the criminal there is the potential
of a high reward with little risk.

